# {{ project_name }} — Google OSS-Fuzz onboarding

This directory stages the files for hosted, continuous fuzzing on
[Google OSS-Fuzz](https://google.github.io/oss-fuzz/). It exists **only in
Apache-2.0 repos**: OSS-Fuzz accepts open-source projects only, so PolyForm-
Noncommercial repos are ineligible and rely on ClusterFuzzLite alone (per-PR, in
CI — see `tests/fuzz/README.md`). The same `tests/fuzz/fuzz_*.py` harnesses feed
both tiers.

## Contents

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `project.yaml` | OSS-Fuzz project metadata: language, `main_repo`, `primary_contact`, sanitizers (address + undefined), libFuzzer engine. |
| `Dockerfile` | Build image from `gcr.io/oss-fuzz-base/base-builder-python`. |
| `build.sh` | Installs `.[fuzz]` and runs `compile_python_fuzzer` over every harness. |

## One-time onboarding (do this ONCE per repo)

1. Confirm this repo is genuinely public and Apache-2.0. Non-OSS repos are not accepted.
2. Fork [`google/oss-fuzz`](https://github.com/google/oss-fuzz) and create
   `projects/{{ project_slug }}/`.
3. Copy the three files from this directory into that folder:
   `project.yaml`, `Dockerfile`, `build.sh`.
4. In the copied `Dockerfile`, replace `COPY . $SRC/project` with
   `RUN git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/{{ github_owner }}/{{ project_slug }} $SRC/project`
   so the hosted builder clones the repo (the COPY form is only for local
   `infra/helper.py build_fuzzers {{ project_slug }}` testing).
5. Verify locally before opening the PR:
   ```bash
   python infra/helper.py build_fuzzers --sanitizer address {{ project_slug }}
   python infra/helper.py check_build {{ project_slug }}
   ```
6. Open the onboarding PR to `google/oss-fuzz`. Once merged, OSS-Fuzz fuzzes the
   harnesses continuously and emails `primary_contact` on findings.

After onboarding, new harnesses added under `tests/fuzz/` are picked up
automatically — no further OSS-Fuzz PR is needed.
